      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Destination Delivery Handover for Two‑Wheeler & Motorcycle</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The handover at the destination is the final checkpoint that guarantees the vehicle reaches the customer in the exact condition documented at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It combines visual verification, mileage confirmation, and formal sign‑off to protect both the logistics provider and the buyer.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process is performed in daylight to ensure accurate visual assessment and must be recorded in writing.</span></li></ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Bring the vehicle into a well‑lit area; natural daylight eliminates shadows that can hide scratches or dents.</li>
        <li>Compare the vehicle side‑by‑side with the original pickup photographs. Verify that paintwork, body panels, lights, mirrors, and accessories match the images.</li>
        <li>Note any new blemishes, missing parts, or wear that was not present at pickup. Document each discrepancy with a photo and a brief description.</li>
        <li>Use a standardized checklist to ensure no area is overlooked: front, rear, wheels, fuel tank, exhaust, and any custom fittings.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Odometer Verification Against the LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Read the odometer on the instrument cluster and record the exact mileage.</li>
        <li>Cross‑check this reading with the mileage recorded on the Lorry Receipt (LR) bilty, which captures the vehicle’s distance at the time of loading.</li>
        <li>If the odometer shows a higher reading, calculate the difference and confirm that it aligns with the distance traveled during transit.</li>
        <li>Any unexplained variance must be investigated immediately and noted on the handover form.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Present the completed inspection checklist, photographic evidence, and odometer comparison to the customer.</li>
        <li>Explain any noted discrepancies and obtain the customer’s acknowledgment.</li>
        <li>Both the delivery representative and the customer sign the condition report, confirming that the vehicle has been received in the documented state.</li>
        <li>Provide the customer with a copy of the signed report and retain the original for company records and future reference.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Following this structured handover ensures transparency, reduces post‑delivery disputes, and upholds the integrity of the logistics chain. By conducting a daylight re‑inspection, verifying mileage against the LR bilty, and securing a signed condition sign‑off, all parties can confidently close the delivery transaction.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


